{title: Wellspring of Life}
{subtitle: John 4:14}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The well is [Bb]deep and the sun is [Gm7]high
You [Eb]have nothing to draw with, [F]I ask you why
Who gave [Bb]this water that you [Gm7]hold so tight
Are [Eb]you greater than the father of the light [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Eb]Jacob gave us the [F]well and drank from it [Gm7]himself
With his sons and [Eb]his livestock in [Fsus4]the [Bb]field
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Everyone who drinks this water [Gm7]will be thirsty again
[Eb]But whoever drinks the water I [Fsus4]give will never thirst a[Gm7]gain
The water I give [Eb]will become in them [Cm7]a spring
[Fsus4]Welling up to e[Bb]ter[Bb]nal life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Sir give me this water [Gm7]so I will not get thir[Eb]sty
And have to keep coming here [Fsus4]to draw water from [Bb]the earth
You see the need in [Gm7]my hands and in [Eb]my soul
A deep desire that the [Fsus4]world cannot hold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Eb]Jacob gave us the well [Fsus4]and drank from it him[Gm7]self
With his sons and his [Eb]livestock in the [Fsus4]field
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Everyone who drinks this water will be [Gm7]thirsty again
But who[Eb]ever drinks the water I give will [Fsus4]never thirst again
The [Gm7]water I give will be[Eb]come in them a spring
[Cm7]Welling [Fsus4]up to eternal [Bb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Go call your husband and [Fsus4]come back here
[Gm7]But I have no husband I [Fsus4]tell you dear
You are [Eb]right in saying you have no hus[Fsus4]band
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bbmaj7/A][Eb]A spring of [Fsus4]water welling up
[Eb]To eternal [Bb]life
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
